  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す is transitive.\n\nASPECT (ている): {巻|ま}き{戻|もど}している describes the action of rewinding in progress.\n\nUSAGE: Originally a physical action (rewinding cassette tapes, film reels), {巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す is now commonly used for digital media and figuratively for turning back time.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [tape/video/time]を{巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す (to rewind something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- テープを{巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す: to rewind a tape\n- {時間|じかん}を{巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す: to turn back time\n- {動画|どうが}を{巻|ま}き{戻|もど}す: to rewind a video",
